{
  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 results (config_031, 048, 032, 019) all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile and score 0.706–0.725, with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion showing a small edge. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for that encoder pair are already tested, so no further gains are expected from that exact pair. The next-best untested direction is scvi_n200 + resnet50 + multiprofile, which retains the strongest RNA encoder and the preferred transformer/weighted settings while swapping to the cheaper image encoder. Question: Does the scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted combination remain competitive (expected ~0.70–0.71 based on the ~0.017 resnet50-vs-ViT penalty observed with scgpt), and can it confirm that the current best (0.725) is robust? Why this experiment: Among all untested configs, config_025 has the highest expected accuracy because it combines the three individually best-performing choices (scvi_n200, transformer, weighted) with multiprofile; the only compromise is resnet50. It is also relatively cheap—expected ~3–4 GPU hours (comparable to config_031's 3.60 h, slightly less than imagenet_vit_l transformer runs), making it a cost-efficient final probe. Since this is experiment 10/10 and the best accuracy found so far (0.725, config_031) will stand unless beaten, this is the single untested configuration most likely to challenge that record."
}

